NOT PATCHED. morph.js still writes window.renderFrame and window.anchorAt and
still falls back to getElementById('c') when renderFrame is handed no canvas.
DeckSmith always hands it the mounted canvas, and allows ONE piece per deck
(src/emit/composition.ts refuses a second by name), so those two globals have a
single writer. Lifting that limit means patching morph.js and testing two pieces
on one page — record the patch here when it happens.

Only the cut-paper style is vendored. Riso and pixel read pixels back from the
canvas (getImageData), which flips Chrome's 2D raster mode; core.js, morph.js
and cut-paper.js call it zero times. See
.planning/2026-10-09-animate-piece-design.md and
.planning/2026-10-09-animate-piece-spike.md.

src/build/piece.ts assembles these, in animate's own build order (head, core,
style, the author's scenes and bridges, morph), into each piece's script.
Nothing else of animate is used: no head.html, board, score or tools.
